  "title": "Kirby Problem 4.82",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $\\phi$ be a self-diffeomorphism of a closed, simply-connected, smooth 4-manifold X. Suppose that for every smooth surface $\\Sigma$ in X, the surfaces $\\Sigma$ and $\\phi(\\Sigma)$ are smoothly isotopic.\n\n(a) Is $\\phi$ necessarily smoothly isotopic to the identity map?\n\n(b) Is $\\phi smoothly$ isotopic to a diffeomorphism that is supported on $a B^{4} \\subset X$?",
